<title>SINGAPORE: MidEast crude term prices update -- ADNOC prices.</title>
<headline>MidEast crude term prices update -- ADNOC prices.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest round of Middle East term crude prices began over the weekend with the release of prices by the Abu Dhabi National Oil Co (ADNOC), traders said.</p>
<p>As reported on Reuter on Sunday, ADNOC raised its official selling prices retroactively for May by $1.70/$2.00 per barrel.</p>
<p>The following table shows the latest official selling prices and their differential to the quoted Dubai average price for May, which traders use a gauge of relative value.</p>
<p>		     (Prices are per barrel)</p>
<p>						   Differential to Dubai</p>
<p>		  May     April   Change   May     April   Change</p>
<p>MURBAN	  $20.00  $18.30  +$1.70   +$1.45  +$1.67  (-$0.22)</p>
<p>LOWER ZAKUM   $20.05  $18.35  +$1.70   +$1.50  +$1.72  (-$0.22)</p>
<p>UMM SHAIF     $19.75  $18.05  +$1.70   +$1.20  +$1.42  (-$0.22)</p>
<p>UPPER ZAKUM   $18.70  $16.70  +$2.00   +$0.15  +$0.07  (+$0.08)</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
</text>
